move over sound of music take a hike  mother teresa cause there's a new  christian  in town  yes hbo europe's 30 coins gives us the  most frightening thing to come out of  spain since  antonio banderas played the phantom  [Music]  so come and join me in this sunday  school lesson as i explain  what exactly happened in that ending who  father vergara and father  angelo really are and what might be in  store for season two  but before we begin make sure to like  and subscribe or you'll burn in hell  the last episode is called sacrificio  and if my high school spanish is any  good that means  sacrifice and just like jesus sacrificed  himself for  our sins so too does father manuel  vergara but we'll get into that in a bit  the small spanish town of pedraza is  under the control of father angelo who  has spent the last few years collecting  the 30 coins to usher in a new era of  sin the 30 coins are the roman coins  given to judas for betraying jesus an  event which is depicted in the  introductory titles it is said whoever  holds all 30 will wield a weapon of  unimaginable power which would usher in  a new  world order  napoleon once held three of these coins  and hitler five  so imagine what all 30 could do in  episode 3 we learn of the order of the  canigs the group that wants to collect  all these artifacts they're led by a  catholic priest father fabio santoro a  man who lusts for power and knowledge of  the unknown  his order even has a whole room devoted  to the gospels that  didn't make it into the bible and other  forbidden texts  among these are the three gifts the magi  gave to jesus on his birth but they're  not gold frankincense and myrrh like the  bible would tell you  their magic spells the miracles jesus  performed  weren't miracles they were spells  but who really are these members of the  order of the canines and why would they  want to commit evil  according to father vergara the order  believes that by doing evil they are  following god's divine plan  the logic goes something like this if  god is all-powerful then he should be  able to stop  sickness war poverty basically all that  evil stuff  but he doesn't therefore evil must be a  part of god's divine plan  so by doing evil you're basically  playing a necessary role in god's plan  the order also follows an alternative  view of jesus's death put forward in the  gospel of judas a real document said to  have been written somewhere in the 3rd  century a.d and discovered in the 1970s  it's important to note that you can't  find this gospel in the bible but if  you're interested you can  find it online it details that judas  wasn't a betrayer but that jesus knew he  was to die and asked judas to betray him  so that he could be sacrificed  we also have this guy named angelo or  angel the entity who ends up  orchestrating the collection of the  coins and prepares everything for  fabio's ascension  as the dark pope he never explicitly  says he's the devil but he definitely  could be his name has angel in it and  satan was an angel who rebelled against  god  in episode 3 we get a flashback of  vergara santoro and sandro in 1990.  santoro has chained angelo in a storage  unit for over two months and this angelo  guy  claims god is a madman who enjoys  watching humans suffer  after the great battle between satan and  god satan withdrew his men to a safe  place hiding in an aspect of god  called hell this battle erupted because  the angels who were tasked with  committing evil by god  were never given credit for their part  in god's divine plan  they're kind of like the judases of the  afterlife constantly being blamed for  bad things even though they're just  doing what they've been told  god of course couldn't allow the  rebellious angels into the control of  satan to get credit because  that would mean exposing their evil as  part of himself  what i'm getting at here is that god is  basically good  and evil it's a delicate balancing act  but with the 30 coins the koenigs want  to tip the balance of power in their  favor the last episode begins with  father angelo awaiting the arrival of  fabio santoro they soon  to be dark pope i guess they need a  human to fill this role kind of like how  jesus filled that role for god  he's created a fog around the town using  a spell involving the blood of unborn  children which forbids anyone from  leaving  he's also mind controlled almost all the  town's people via unholy communion  anyone who takes communion falls under  his control we see this when mercy isn't  under his control opting to save her  communion wafers vergara arrives back in  town to face his demons  literally in a very weird battle with a  giant hell demon that drops burned  hellspawn he shoots a version of himself  after which the creature disappears but  why would vergara's soul  be in hell as we'll find out later  vergara has been working this entire  time for satan in the season's climax  angelo reveals that vergara was  chosen by him he needed someone who  could resist temptation all these years  without crumbling under the pressure  someone who could hold on to the coin  for safe keeping  and not give into its power until he was  needed it's never revealed in the show  why angelo couldn't hold on to the coin  himself it's only hinted that the coin  will always find a way out of hell  because it doesn't want to be there  that's why he needed someone on earth to  hold it for him this is also why he has  minions like father lagrange or  manipulate others to steal the coins  in episode five it's hinted that vergara  is like the judas of the canites  this man has betrayed his loved ones  too for the sake of our cause  father centauro says vergara sacrificed  everything his family his friends his  job  even spent years in prison for the sake  of protecting the coin  this man has protected for years the  holy coin of betrayal with his life  but vergara has no idea what's going on  he believes he's protecting the coin  from the order not holding it for them  after all angelo didn't give him the  coin he got it during a botched exorcism  years ago one which saw a young boy  named giacomo  die of a heart attack and vergara being  sent to jail what he didn't know was  that giacomo was angelo and  angelo is giacomo the devil can take  many forms as is evidenced in one of the  final scenes where we see his reflection  change  the dark pope ends up stabbing vergara  with a spear of longinus the spear that  stabbed christ as he hung from the cross  and there is a lot of symbolism  throughout the series of vergara being  christ-like if you can get past the fact  he kills a lot of people like him being  referred to as the chosen one  bloody palms like jesus's hands being  nailed on the cross  or even godlike powers that allow him to  snap a knife with his bare hands  i don't remember jesus doing that in the  bible but if he did i sure as hell would  have paid more attention  with all 30 coins set within the dark  pope's hat fabio centauro addresses the  crowd of gathered canites signaling the  beginning of the end  but vergara has one more trick up his  sleeve earlier in the episode he used  the blood of saint ambrose to conjure a  spell and take control of a dove he uses  this dove to distract fabio allowing him  to sacrifice himself by throwing him off  the edge of the church the dark pope's  hat falls off scattering the coins  everywhere causing the canines to  viciously fight for their control  now this is absolutely setting us up for  a season 2 essentially resetting the  coins to be found  all over again and that's exactly what  happens with mercy who conveniently  finds one underneath her shoe with her  being rejected by  paco it looks like she'll be teaming up  with father lagrange who seemed to be  flirting with her earlier in the episode  to possibly collect the coins all over  again  now we have to ask ourselves is father  vergara dead  i wouldn't count on it with all the  christ symbolism  resurrection spells angels and whatnot  in this show i wouldn't count them out  the guy also fell from a height shorter  than antonio did in episode one and  antonio survived so who knows then  there's elena who was stabbed with a  cursed pin  normally something this size wouldn't  kill you but since it was cursed by the  cockroach lady it seems to be far more  dangerous  the question that remains is if the  curse will have any lingering effects  like will it make it so paco and elena  can't fall in love because  as the old lady said to mercy now he's  all yours  finally i want to talk about angelo  morphing into this asian man i checked  the credits and he's simply referred to  as  asiatico or asian judging by this and  the actors  slim imdb credits over the years i don't  think this is some big new character for  season 2  really the purpose of this last scene is  to show us two things  that angelo can morph into different  forms and that he has business in new  york  but check this out if you pause here you  can tell it's not  an asian man did they not have money to  fly the actor out to new york or has  angelo shape-shifted once again  other than that there's not much to go  on but if i were to guess what the main  plot of season 2 will be  it's three groups vying to collect the  30 coins  we have paco elena and vergara as group  1 lagrange and mercy as group 2  and angelo as group 3. so i'm excited to  see how this plays out but what did you  think of 30  coins and do you have any theories on  season 2 let me know in the comments  below  thanks for watching everyone please make  sure to like subscribe and share and for  more bad takes you can follow me on  twitter and instagram at thinkstoryyt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much
 

